  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Prakash Rathor vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 January, 2026 Neutral Citation No. 2026:Mphc-Jbp:5594 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Sandeep N. Bhatt On The 20th Of January, 2026 Writ Petition No. 13653 of 2012 Prakash Rathor And Others Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh And Others Appearance: Shri Abhishek Arjaria - Advocate for the petitioner. Shri Tapan Bathre - Panel Lawyer for the State. Order The present petition is filed praying the following reliefs: \"(i) To allow the petition by setting aside the order dated 26/05/2012 (Annex.P-5) passed by the Adjudicating Officer and consequently petitioners be acquitted.",
    "facts": "It is seen that under the Food Safety Act action is taken and the Food item and vehicle used on certain occasion are seized and applications are filed for seeking release of the vehicle or the seized item on Supurtagi. The specified authority in various cases expressed their inability to release the vehicle on the ground that they do not have such a power under the statute and when the application is filed before the Chief Judicial Magistrate or the Magistrate concerned they are also not interfering as there is no Court specified or constituted, for dealing with the case. The aggrieved persons are left remedyless in the matter . Today when the matter is taken up, learned counsel for the parties jointly submitted that now the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal as required under Sections 70 and 74 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is notified and the concerned Sessions Court in each district is notified as the appellate tribunal.",
